      "changeSets": {
        "1": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 176,
                "quote": "| Some _ -> Error(InvalidInput $\"{path} already exists\")"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new 'never overwrite a backup' rule is decided only in the Tier 3 use case `backup`. No Tier 1/2 function holds it. It concerns archive handling, not a lending rule, and it contradicts nothing in Tier 2, so I scored it 1 instead of 0. `restore` and `backup-info` apply no domain rules. The summary counts and the owed total come from Tier 2 (`Accounts.owed`) and Tier 1 collections. Moving the backup call from the CLI into a use case also removes a presentation-to-persistence shortcut.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The old CLI code called `JsonFileStore.create path` directly. The change replaces it with `UseCases.backup`, `restore` and `backupInfo`, which reach the file system only through the existing `ports.Archive` and `ports.Store`. No new port was needed. Tier 1/2 gained no effects, and the CLI only parses input and renders views. This removes an existing Tier 4 presentation-to-persistence violation instead of adding one.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The 'no backup at' error is defined once in `noBackup` and shared by `restore` and `backupInfo`. The summary text is built once in `Views.summary` and `showSummary`. The owed total reuses `Accounts.owed` and `money`, so no policy value is copied.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 22,
                "quote": "let restoreMember memberId (backup: Library) (library: Library) : Result<Library * Member, LendingError> ="
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The legality checks are in Tier 2 `Accounts.restoreMember`: the member must exist in the backup, and the member must not already exist in the current library. It also decides what is restored (fines and payments only, no loans, holds or reminders). The Tier 3 `restoreMember` only loads the backup, calls Tier 2 inside `commit`, and maps the result to a view. The CLI only formats the output.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The backup is read through `ports.Archive.Load`, and the state change goes through the existing `commit` helper. `Accounts.restoreMember` is pure and does no I/O. The CLI only calls the use case and renders its result, and does not call Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The change reuses the `noBackup` error and the existing `DuplicateMember` error, so those facts have one definition each. The fines and payments are selected through `Accounts.finesOf` and `paymentsOf`. The view recounts them from the same source, so the two cannot drift. No literals or predicates are copied.",
            "score": 2
          }
        }
